cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SDPX.jl in academic work, please cite it as below."
title: "SDPX.jl: an arbitrary-precision primal-dual interior-point SDP solver in Julia"
abstract: >-
  SDPX.jl is a native Julia semidefinite programming solver using the
  primal-dual interior-point method with the HRVW/KSH/M search direction and a
  Mehrotra predictor-corrector. It supports Float64, BigFloat, MultiFloats and
  DoubleFloats arithmetic, multithreaded kernels, sparse and arrow-structured
  KKT paths, and a MathOptInterface/JuMP wrapper. It is a substantial rewrite of
  SDPJSolver.jl and is motivated by the S-matrix/EFT bootstrap, the modular
  bootstrap, and the lattice bootstrap.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Yongjun
    family-names: Xu
    email: yongjunx23@gmail.com
version: 0.5.0-DEV
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/yongjunx23-del/SDPX.jl"
keywords:
  - semidefinite programming
  - interior-point method
  - arbitrary precision
  - S-matrix bootstrap
  - modular bootstrap
  - lattice bootstrap
  - Julia
references:
